  postAuthor: Josephine Njoroge
  authorImage: {fileID: 0}
  postHeader: 
  postContent: "Citing unnamed \u201Cinsiders,\u201D this report labels every policy
    as \u201Crigged\u201D or \u201Ccorrupt\u201D without presenting official statements
    or documents\u2014casting doubt on the entire administration.\n"
  funFact_Hint: Think about how word choice shapes your opinion before you see the
    facts.
  BiasChoices:
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 1
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: "It uses loaded words (\u201Crigged,\u201D \u201Ccorrupt\u201D)
      to slant perception against the administration. \n"
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 6
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: 'This is about narrative tone, not who gets to
      speak. '
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 4
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: "Confirmation bias cherry-picks evidence; here
      it\u2019s the tone, not selective data. \n"
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 3
  - <IsCorrectAnswer>k__BackingField: 0
    <Explanation>k__BackingField: 'While dramatic, the tactic is more about slanted
      framing than pure hype.


'
    <Choice>k__BackingField: 1
